attr[seg000:1f64]: name = actions_time_in_day_4; comment = [[[
    Time-of-day 4 action: the Harkonnen sietch raid scheduler. Arms once
    game_time has passed data_01154 by 0x70 (or unconditionally from phase
    0x3c), fires only on even days (game_time bit 4 clear), is suppressed for
    one firing by data_011bc, and needs a set rolling rand bit. A raid picks a
    target via harkonnen_pick_attack_target, bumps ds:c4, moves up to two
    troops from the source area onto the target (occupation 0x8d, re-homed via
    troop_location_084a6 / troop_08357), battle-flags the target (status bit 1),
    queues vision message 0xC/0xD ("The Harkonnens are attacking ...!"), and -
    when the target is the current location - enters the night attack
    (night_attack_stage, location_06144); otherwise resolves it off-screen
    (location_05d50).
]]]
attr[seg000:1fd5]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:1fe7]: comment = Send message type C = "The Harkonnens are attacking ...!"
attr[seg000:1fe9]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:1ff1]: comment = Send message type D = "The Harkonnens are attacking ...! Be careful Muad'Dib, the prospecting troop might be involved in the fight."
attr[seg000:2017]: type = code; name = harkonnen_pick_attack_target; ofs_seg = seg001; fn = out location: *Location @di, out zf: *bool @zf; comment = [[[
    Pick the sietch the Harkonnen raid tonight (actions_time_in_day_4). Scans
    sietch locations (appearance < 0x20) that are not hidden/battle-flagged
    (status bits 0x82 clear), house no ill troop, and have the lowest [di+4]
    seen (starting threshold 100); each candidate is CONDIT-staged to read the
    ds:60 skill array and the Harkonnen-distance words: it qualifies only when
    ds:60[0] != ds:60[3] and either a Harkonnen area is within 30 (ds:e2) or the
    nearest one (ds:dc/ds:de) is, and the staging location is not the Carthag
    palace. Returns the target in di (0 = none, ZF set) with the source area in
    bp (data_0d818); also latches the target into _unk_2CCC6_comm_glow_index.
]]]
attr[seg000:201a]: let = location: *Location @di
attr[seg000:205d]: ofs_seg = seg001; comment = Atreides (Carthag) palace.
attr[seg000:20a4]: name = actions_time_in_day_3; comment = [[[
    Time-of-day 3 action: the spice-shipment day counter. Armed by ds:bf bit 7.
    Before the shipment event day (data_0118d) it keeps days_left_until_spice_
    shipment (ds:cf) updated; on the day itself (with bit 4 clear) it rolls a
    new demand: quantity ds:bc = (sequence ds:c3 * 150 + 100) * (rand(0..0x3f)
    + 0xe0) / 256, scaled down by the fulfilment fraction ds:be, arms ds:bf
    bits 4+7, and posts COMM sighting (0x20b/0x30b). While a demand is pending
    (bit 4 set) days 1..3 after the event day post the escalating reminder
    sightings from the 0x2161 table (person 0x0b); day 4+, or an unpaid flag
    data_011bb, requests room-screen type 7 (loc_0215f) - the shipment
    consequence.
]]]
