attr[seg000:37b2]: name = draw_room_scene; comment = [[[
    Render the current location/room scene into the game area: resets the clip rect
    and clears the game area, then draws the room sprites (calls into draw_SAL,
    seg000:3b59). The higher-level orchestrator used by draw_room_game_screen.
]]]
attr[seg000:3805]: targets = segvga:017b
attr[seg000:380c]: name = draw_outdoor_backdrop; comment = [[[
    The outdoor view drawn as (or behind) the scene, reached via loc_037eb from
    both draw_room_scene dispatches (the first-room path seg000:3a02..3a16 and
    the desert branch loc_037dc). Installs the sky-gradient palette
    (set_sky_palette), picks a full-screen backdrop sheet and draws its sprite 0
    (loc_0c2f2). al = the distance the nearby location (last_location_ptr) is
    seen from: 0 in a room (bl == 0x80); in the desert the fine latitude when
    standing on the location's longitude (seg000:382d dx == [si+2]). Below
    room1_backdrop_threshold the resource is room1_backdrop_base[calc_SAL_index]
    + al (DP1/DP0/DP2/DP3 for the palace — the view recedes step by step; the
    VILG base 0x7f varies by first_name at seg000:383f); past it (or off the
    longitude) loc_0384a hashes the position into a DN20..DN38 dune tile or a
    VG01..VG10 rock tile when the surrounding map bytes are rock terrain.
]]]
