attr[seg000:3b59]: type = code; name = draw_SAL; comment = [[[
    Draw one SAL room chunk: (background-1) >> 4 picks the sprite-sheet resource
    (0x13 + n), (background-1) & 0xf the SAL sub-chunk. Sheet index 0 (GENERIC.HSQ)
    is NEVER opened here (seg000:3b68 jz skips the open_resource_by_index): GENERIC
    stays resident through the font path (font_draw_glyph_func opens 0x13 for every
    glyph), so its palette chunk (240..254, the sand UI tint) is not applied by the
    room draw and the sky palette time-of-day UI span survives. Then walk the chunk:
    sprite entries (cmd/x/y/pal_offset), 0xffff terminator, high-bit person entries
    (sal_draw_character_entry).
]]]
attr[seg000:3b6d]: comment = RES_GENERIC_HSQ
attr[seg000:3b7b]: comment = Fetch SAL subchunk offset. ds:si points to chunk
attr[seg000:3b80]: comment = Fetch word from SAL chunk
attr[seg000:3b84]: comment = If -1 goto
attr[seg000:3b86]: comment = If high bit set, goto
attr[seg000:3b88]: comment = ah = flags, al = sprite_index
attr[seg000:3b8c]: comment = grab second-lowest bit from flags and combine with sprite x
attr[seg000:3b90]: comment = dx = sprite x
attr[seg000:3b95]: comment = bx = sprite y
