attr[seg000:4415]: type = code; name = map_screen_cleanup; comment = [[[
    The map screen elements cleanup func (the bx passed to the screen-element
    push at seg000:430b). Guarded by exchanging data_046eb with 0: clears the
    visible-location list head (data_0a5c0), the mouse hotspot, the marker and
    select-destination frame tasks, restores the room backdrop (loc_043e3), drops
    game_screen_mode_flags unless a travel is pending (data_011c5), reselects the
    room mouse handlers and nav panel, and with a destination armed
    (data_04728 > 0) enters the travel departure (loc_049d4).
]]]
attr[seg000:4429]: ofs_seg = seg000
attr[seg000:445d]: name = map_arm_player_marker_task; ofs_seg = seg000; comment = [[[
    Arm the blinking "you are here" marker: remove the blink task, project the
    players map position (get_map_position ->
    map_position_to_screen_if_visible; off-window clears map_player_marker_rect
    and bails), read ICONES sprite 0x4c s header for its size, store the marker
    bounding rect (x-13, y-height)..(+width, +height) into map_player_marker_rect,
    re-add map_player_marker_blink_task at interval 0x12c, zero the phase, and
    fall into the task body for the immediate first draw.
]]]
attr[seg000:448f]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:449d]: ofs_seg = seg000
attr[seg000:44ab]: type = code; name = map_player_marker_blink_task; comment = [[[
    The blinking "you are here" map marker: each firing bumps
    map_player_marker_phase, restores the marker rect (clamped to the map window)
    from fb1 to the screen (present_screen_rect_regs), and on odd phases draws
    ICONES sprite 0x4c at the rects origin clipped to the map window — so the
    marker alternates visible/hidden. Draws to the front buffer, bracketed by the
    cursor restore/redraw.
]]]
attr[seg000:44bc]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:44cd]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:44d0]: let = rect: *Rect @si
attr[seg000:450e]: type = code; name = map_mouse_lmb_select_destination; fn = in x: u16 @dx, in y: u16 @bx; comment = [[[
    The map screen's LMB handler: select the hovered travel destination.
    Inert unless a map mode is active (game_screen_mode_flags & 0x0f) and the
    hover state (refreshed via map_mouse_hover_tracker) is nonzero; a hovered
    location marker is also inert when it is the player's current location
    (current_location_ptr), unless mode flags & 3. Plays the destination's
    narration clip with the score ducked, blinks the hover label 9 times
    (0x14 ticks off / 0x0a ticks on), waits out the clip, sets data_04732 =
    0x80 and enters the travel-confirm chain (loc_04703).
]]]
attr[seg000:456c]: name = map_hover_narration_clip; fn = in hover: u16 @di, out clip: u16 @ax; comment = [[[
    Map a map-hover state to its narration voice clip index: a location ptr
    gives 0x2bc + (first_name - 1) * 16 + last_name; the 0xffXX desert states
    add 0x2bc with 16-bit wrap (0xffff -> 0x2bb, 0xfff0+n -> 0x2ac+n).
]]]
attr[seg000:4586]: name = map_mouse_hover_tracker; fn = in x: u16 @dx, in y: u16 @bx; comment = [[[
    The map screen's idle/drag mouse handler: recompute the hover state into
    data_046fc, redrawing the hover label strip (map_draw_hover_label) when it
    changes. States: 0 = pointer outside the map window; a location ptr =
    within 9 pixels (Manhattan) of that visible location marker; 0xfff0+n =
    aligned within ~4 degrees of compass point n (0 N .. 7 NW) out from the
    player marker's tip (marker rect x0+11, y1); otherwise 0xffff.
]]]
attr[seg000:45de]: name = map_draw_hover_label; fn = in hover: u16 @di; comment = [[[
    Draw the map hover label strip to the front buffer in the small font: pen
    (0x55, 0x22) colour word 0xf5fe, or (0x55, 0x26) / 0x20fe in ornithopter
    mode. hover = a location ptr: its type string + name ("Sietch: Tuono-Tabr");
    0xfff0+n: "DESERT" + a space + the compass-point phrase 0xda+n; 0xffff:
    "DESERT" alone; 0: nothing (and the select-destination caption typewriter
    is re-armed; every other state removes it). The strip is space-padded
    until the pen passes x 0xed, erasing the previous label.
]]]
attr[seg000:460f]: comment = "DESERT"
attr[seg000:461c]: targets = seg000:d096, seg000:d0ff, seg000:d12f, seg000:d16a
attr[seg000:4625]: comment = "northwards", etc.
attr[seg000:464b]: targets = seg000:d096, seg000:d0ff, seg000:d12f, seg000:d16a
attr[seg000:4658]: name = map_add_select_destination_text_task; comment = [[[
    Arm the map caption typewriter unless already armed (data_0473f != 0):
    resolve string 0x57 "SELECT DESTINATION ON MAP" into the data_0473f/data_04741
    far pointer, pen x = 0x55 into data_04743, pen y and colour word into
    data_04745/data_04747 (globe mode y 0x22, colours 0xf561; ornithopter mode
    y 0x26, colours 0x2061), and add the map_caption_frame_task at interval 0x18.
    The task then writes the caption one letter per firing.
]]]
attr[seg000:4665]: comment = "SELECT DESTINATION ON MAP"
attr[seg000:468e]: ofs_seg = seg000
attr[seg000:469b]: name = map_remove_select_destination_text_task; comment = [[[
    Disarm the map caption typewriter: when data_0473f != 0, clear it and remove
    the map_caption_frame_task.
]]]
attr[seg000:46ab]: ofs_seg = seg000
attr[seg000:46b5]: type = code; name = map_caption_frame_task; comment = [[[
    The map caption typewriter: each firing draws ONE glyph of the string at
    data_0473f:data_04741 to the front buffer at the data_04743/data_04745 pen in
    the small font with the data_04747 colour word, advancing the pointer and
    storing the pen back. A space costs no firing (seg000:46fe loops straight to
    the next glyph); a high-bit byte is the string terminator (the task then
    idles until removed). The draw is bracketed by the cursor restore/redraw
    (restore_mouse_if_rect_intersects on the data_014a4 strip /
    draw_mouse_cursor_if_needed).
]]]
attr[seg000:46c4]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:4703]: name = map_confirm_travel_and_close; comment = [[[
    The travel-confirm chain (entered from the destination click at
    seg000:4569 and SKIP TO DESTINATION at seg000:5116): arm the pending
    travel (arm_pending_travel), refresh the sky, fold the map mode bit into
    the travel bit (flags |= flags >> 2), reselect the music, cancel a staged
    night attack (loc_00b21), and pop the map screen element (the cleanup
    keeps the mode flags while travel_destination_ptr is set). First-confirm
    (old flags & 3 == 0): reset travel_step_counter, un-grey SKIP TO
    DESTINATION, fold the HUD head (orni mode), snapshot the restored room to
    fb2, run the departure NPC scans, play the departure transition
    (preserving travel_heading around it), force a scene rebuild
    (current_scene = 0xff), take the first travel step, detach
    current_location_ptr, zero travel_step_tick_stamp, rebuild the room view
    (loc_02dbf) and arm the travel pump (data_04727 = 0xff); orni mode then
    decrements the pads ornithopter count and stops the voice. Otherwise (or
    non-orni) redraw the command panel and flush the palette.
]]]
attr[seg000:4795]: type = code; name = play_travel_departure_transition; fn = in old_mode_flags: u8 @al; comment = [[[
    Play the departure transition for the mode the map screen was entered
    from (al = the pre-confirm game_screen_mode_flags). Nothing on the full
    globe (data_046eb bit 0x80). al == 4 (the ornithopter map): prefetch the
    flight HNMs (prefetch_travel_hnm_resources), and when the destination
    click armed data_04732 bit 7, fold the HUD head away, re-render the scene
    without the parked ornis (orni_anim_frame = 0xff) snapshotting it to fb2,
    start the SN6.VOC engine loop and run the takeoff animation
    (orni_anim_loop, cl = 1). Any other al: set game phase 0x50 with its
    transition (seg000:47a0..47ca, the worm/globe flows).
]]]
attr[seg000:47b7]: ofs_seg = seg000
attr[seg000:47f6]: comment = Play SN6.VOC
attr[seg000:47fb]: name = orni_anim_loop; ofs_seg = seg000; fn = in step: u8 @cl; comment = [[[
    The ornithopter takeoff/landing animation pump: each pass draws one frame
    (orni_anim_draw_frame via the wait callback), waits 0x14 ticks, steps
    orni_anim_frame by cl (+1 takeoff, -1 landing), releases the SN6 engine
    loop when an upward pass reaches frame 0x1a, and services the MIDI score;
    runs until the frame passes 0x21.
]]]
attr[seg000:4821]: type = code; name = orni_anim_draw_frame; fn = in step: u8 @cl; comment = [[[
    Draw one takeoff/landing frame: restore the clean pad scene from fb2,
    open ORNYTK.HSQ (flushing its bank palette) and draw the animated orni at
    the pad position — past frame 0xe it climbs away (x -= 5 per frame,
    mirrored by the step sign; y -= (frame-0xe)^2 / 2) — plus the ornis still
    parked beyond the departing slot (the step-first draw_ornis entry, at anim
    frame 0), then present the game area. Frame 0xd also releases the
    engine-sound loop; a running sky fade keeps stepping.
]]]
attr[seg000:4828]: comment = RES_ORNYTK_HSQ
attr[seg000:488a]: name = travel_arrival_landing_sequence; comment = [[[
    The orni-arrival landing sequence, run from the scene reload (loc_02dfb, seg000:2e02)
    when data_04732 bit 0 is set by the travel arrival. Branches on
    calc_SAL_index(current_location):
    - < 8 (sietch/village/palace types): hide the minimap (travel_minimap_state = 0x80),
      pump flight frames forcing sand terrain (travel_select_flight_video al=0) until the
      clip loops back to MNT1 (hnm_video_id == 2), wait for hnm_counter_2 to reach 0x3c
      (SAL type 6) / 0x16 (others), then hnm_switch_active_video(bx = the SAL index = the
      approach video id: 6 SIET, 7 PALACE, ...) and play the approach clip to completion;
      then data_046e0--, data_04732 = 0 and open_SAL_resource.
    - == 9: play the current clip to completion full-screen (loc_0c8fb).
    - else (the landing-pad types): the reverse orni landing animation (orni_anim frames
      0x1f down to 0, SN7.VOC).
]]]
attr[seg000:48dd]: ofs_seg = seg000
attr[seg000:4904]: comment = Play SN7.VOC
attr[seg000:4913]: type = code; name = callback_transition_04913
attr[seg000:4916]: comment = VER.HNM
attr[seg000:4924]: comment = Play SN8.VOC
attr[seg000:4937]: name = hnm_end_voc_loop_check_complete; comment = [[[
    When the HNM frame counter low byte ([dbe8] _word_2D098_hnm_frame_counter & 0xff) reaches 0x0b, end the
    currently looping VOC via call_pcm_vtable_end_loop (dnsdb_end_loop) so it stops repeating.
    Then tail-call check_if_hnm_complete, returning ZF=clip finished. Called once per advanced
    frame by intro_41_play_VER_HNM (loc_0071d).
]]]
attr[seg000:4944]: name = arm_pending_travel; fn = in hover: u16 @di, in x: u16 @dx, in y: u16 @bx; comment = [[[
    Arm the pending travel from the selected map hover state (di) and the
    click screen position (dx/bx). A desert state (>= 0xfff0) sets
    data_011cb = 0xff, converts the click to a map cell
    (map_screen_to_position) and aims travel_heading at it with
    travel_heading_mode = 1 (fixed heading, destination = last_location_ptr);
    a location ptr aims at the location with mode 0 (re-aimed each step).
    Both commit travel_destination_ptr and seed the step accumulator
    (adjust_travel_heading).
]]]
attr[seg000:4965]: name = travel_aim_at_location; fn = in location: *Location @di; comment = [[[
    Aim the travel at the location record di: the compass angle from the player
    position (compass_angle_to_location), homing mode (cl 0); falls into
    travel_commit_destination.
]]]
attr[seg000:496a]: name = travel_commit_destination; fn = in location: *Location @di, in heading_mode: u8 @cl, in angle: u8 @al; comment = [[[
    Commit the pending travel: travel_destination_ptr = di, travel_heading_mode = cl,
    travel_heading zeroed; the tail jmp adjust_travel_heading lands the al angle in the
    heading and re-seeds the step accumulator to half a cell.
]]]
attr[seg000:497a]: type = code; name = menu_callback_choice_change_destination; comment = [[[
    CHANGE DESTINATION (records data_01fa0/data_021f8): tear down the scene lip-sync,
    set travel_minimap_state 1 (the map-screen cleanup re-enters the flight minimap
    view on close) and reopen the map main view with the Cancel menu
    (bp = menu_multiple_cancel).
]]]
