attr[seg000:5d44]: name = location_mark_map_and_minimap_dirty; fn = in location: *Location @di; comment = [[[
    location_mark_map_view_dirty plus the flight variant: while a travel mode
    is active (game_screen_mode_flags bits 0-1) also flag the minimap redraw
    (travel_minimap_state bit 0).
]]]
attr[seg000:5d50]: name = location_mark_map_view_dirty; fn = in location: *Location @di; comment = [[[
    A location changed in a way the map shows (revealed, battle over, ...):
    while a map view is up (data_046eb nonzero) and the location is visible and
    not hidden, bump the data_046ec dirty counter so the next event-run refresh
    repaints the view.
]]]
attr[seg000:5d6d]: name = map_view_refresh_after_events; comment = [[[
    Refresh the map/globe main view after the time-period event run (called from
    run_events_for_current_time_period at seg000:1b9e, gated on the data_046ec
    dirty counter, which it resets). data_046eb > 0: restore the cursor and jump
    through _word_23B9D_current_main_view_drawing_function; bit 0x80: the full-
    globe redraw path (loc_05d82); 0: fall to loc_05dcd (ret).
]]]
attr[seg000:5d7e]: targets = seg000:4377, seg000:49a0
attr[seg000:5dae]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:5dce]: name = map_build_and_draw_location_markers; comment = [[[
    Rebuild the visible-location marker list (visible_location_markers) and draw
    the markers over the map view. Globe mode (data_046eb bit 0x80) first runs the
    loc_0633b rotated-offset precompute; data_046eb bit 0x40 keeps the lists
    leading non-0x40 entries and rebuilds from the first 0x40-flagged one. Every
    non-hidden location (status bit 0x80 clear) inside the view
    (location_visible_on_map) is appended as [location ptr, screen x, screen y:u8,
    data_046eb:u8] and its marker sprite (calc_location_marker_sprite) drawn
    centred on the screen position, clipped to the map window; sietches
    (appearance < 0x20) farther than location_visibility_distance draw the +5
    distant variant. The list is 0-terminated.
]]]
attr[seg000:5dda]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:5df1]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:5e42]: name = calc_location_marker_sprite; comment = [[[
    The map marker sprite for the location at si: ICONES base 0x3a (windowed) or
    0x7a (globe, data_046eb bit 0x80), tiered by the locations appearance through
    the shared calc_SAL_index thresholds (+0 sietch, +1 Atreides palace,
    +2 village, +3 Harkonnen fortress, +4 Harkonnen palace/special). Returns
    ax = sprite, cl = the appearance byte.
]]]
attr[seg000:5e4f]: type = code; name = calc_SAL_index
attr[seg000:5e57]: comment = Atreides Palace: +1.
attr[seg000:5e5d]: comment = Village: +2.
attr[seg000:5e63]: comment = Harkonnen Fortresses: +3.
attr[seg000:5e69]: comment = Harkonnen Palace and special locations (3A, 7A in the function above): +4.
attr[seg000:5e6b]: type = code
attr[seg000:5e6d]: name = find_nearest_location_marker; fn = in max_appearance: u8 @al, in x: u16 @dx, in y: u16 @bx, out marker_location: u16 @di, out distance: u16 @ax; comment = [[[
    Walk visible_location_markers for the entry nearest (x, y) by Manhattan
    distance. Entries are skipped unless location->appearance < max_appearance
    and the entry's stored mode byte (+5) equals data_046eb. Returns the
    winning location ptr in di (0 if none) and its distance in ax (0xffff if
    none); the first entry wins ties.
]]]
attr[seg000:5e83]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:5ed0]: type = code; name = location_find_visible_marker; ofs_seg = seg001; fn = in location: *Location @di, out zero: bool @zf; comment = [[[
    Find the visible-location marker entry for the location (di): walk
    visible_location_markers (ZF set + bp = the entry).
]]]
attr[seg000:5ee4]: name = map_place_location_panel; fn = in location: *Location @di; comment = [[[
    Place the location info panel next to the locations visible marker
    (location_find_visible_marker), height keyed on the class
    (troop_icon_panel_heights[class]: 88/60/30/0). Re-clicking the same open
    location at the same class just repaints (loc_07b1b). Falls into
    map_place_popup_panel.
]]]
attr[seg000:5ee9]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:5f25]: name = map_place_info_panel; comment = [[[
    Place a popup panel record (si) next to an icon at (dx, bx): 106 px wide,
    cx tall, vertically centred on the icon clamped into [4, 148 - cx]; on the
    right at x+15 unless that crosses x 210, then 130 px left. Registers the
    panel in map_popup_ptr, draws the comm-glow pointer arrow at (x-10, y-10)
    (loc_0c0e8, overlay slot 6) and the panel fill + frame (loc_07b1b).
]]]
attr[seg000:5f6c]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:5f79]: name = map_close_location_troop_popup; comment = [[[
    Close the location troop popup menu (data_046f8): when open and the active
    screen element is not a locked base, exit the menu
    (menu_callback_choice_exit_menu).
]]]
attr[seg000:5f91]: name = map_close_location_popup; comment = [[[
    The GO THERE menus cleanup: clear the location popup gate (data_046f8 /
    data_046f7) and close the info panel (loc_05f9f: clear map_popup_ptr,
    repaint the panel rect).
]]]
attr[seg000:5f9c]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:5fb0]: name = map_click_location_marker; comment = [[[
    An LMB click near a location marker: leave the spice sub-mode (loc_058fa),
    dismiss the open troop popups (map_dismiss_troop_popups), draw the location
    info popup (map_draw_location_popup) and, unless it is the players own
    location, push a GO THERE command menu (cleanup map_close_location_popup):
    the desert offers GO THERE RIDING A WORM once the worm is available
    (bitfield_Paul_events bit 0x40); a shallow room (current_room <= 2 or the
    rooms appearance < 0x20) offers GO THERE FLYING AN ORNI (greyed without an
    orni). Deep inside a location (room > 2 and appearance >= 0x20) shows the
    panel with no menu.
]]]
attr[seg000:5fe1]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:6000]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:6008]: ofs_seg = seg000
attr[seg000:600e]: name = map_draw_location_popup; comment = [[[
    Draw the location info popup to the screen: place the panel next to the
    locations visible marker (location_05ee4, sets data_046f8), the location
    type header + name, then by class (location_06252) the equipment-or-battle
    section (loc_060ac); class 0 with the Paul-events water flag (0x20) also
    draws the water/spice extra (location_0605c). Class 2 shows only the header.
]]]
attr[seg000:605c]: name = location_0605c; fn = in location: *Location @di
attr[seg000:606e]: comment = "water: "
attr[seg000:60ac]: name = map_draw_location_equipment_or_battle; comment = [[[
    The location panels equipment-or-battle section: a Battle: gauge (label
    0x4c, sprite 0x8e + (location_battle_gauge + 0xf)>>5) when the location has
    active combat (location_has_battle), else the Equipment: header (0x6e) and
    the locations own equipment counts (record +0x14) via draw_equipment_row.
]]]
attr[seg000:60c6]: comment = "Equipment:"
attr[seg000:60d9]: comment = "Battle:"
attr[seg000:60f8]: name = location_battle_gauge; fn = in location: *Location @di; comment = [[[
    The locations battle gauge (0..0xff, 0x80 = even): the population-weighted
    balance of the two sides skill. Accumulates over the locations troops
    (troop_accumulate_multiple_things): Sigma field_e / (Sigma field_e + attacker pop)
    vs Sigma field_c / (Sigma field_c + Harkonnen pop), the signed difference over the
    larger, halved and biased +0x80.
]]]
attr[seg000:6102]: ofs_seg = seg000
attr[seg000:6144]: name = location_06144; fn = in location: *Location @di
attr[seg000:6155]: type = code; name = troop_accumulate_battle_sums; fn = in troop: *Troop @si, inout param1: u16 @bx, inout param2: u16 @cx, inout param3: u16 @dx; comment = [[[
    Accumulate a troop into the battle-gauge sums (location_battle_gauge):
    Harkonnen troops (bitfield_10 bit 7) add population to data_0d81c; other
    occupation-6 troops add field_c to param2, field_e to param1, and
    (non-0x20) population to param3.
]]]
attr[seg000:61d3]: name = draw_equipment_column; comment = [[[
    Draw one equipment column: stack cx copies of the ONMAP sprite ax
    vertically from (dx, bx) down toward bp (the panel bottom), squeezing the
    step (min 2) so they fit, then advance dx by the sprite width. Records the
    columns x-range in the dialogue-panel scratch.
]]]
attr[seg000:6231]: type = code; name = get_location_type_string_offset
attr[seg000:6252]: name = location_popup_class; fn = in location: *Location @di; comment = [[[
    The location popup class (0 full, 1 battle, 2 header-only): battle present
    (location_has_battle) -> 1; Atreides -> 2; undiscovered (status bit 4 clear)
    or no type string -> 2; else keyed on the location-type string (type 3 -> 0,
    type 2 -> 1, else 2). Indexes troop_icon_panel_heights for the panel height.
]]]
attr[seg000:627e]: name = location_has_battle; fn = in location: *Location @di; comment = [[[
    The location has active combat: status bit 1 (a battle site), or a
    non-Atreides location with occupation-6 non-Harkonnen troops present
    (location_do_accumulation_on_troops_based_on_occupation dx != 0).
]]]
attr[seg000:629d]: type = code; name = draw_string_location_type
attr[seg000:62a3]: comment = "Sietch: "
