attr[seg000:6715]: name = map_spawn_troop_icons; ofs_seg = seg001; comment = [[[
    Spawn the troop icons for the full map view: for every visible location
    marker, walk the locations troop chain (troop id at location+9, next id at
    troop+1) spawning one icon each (map_spawn_troop_icon); then a second pass
    over troops[] spawns the moving troops (occupation bit 0x40 set,
    bitfield_10 bit 4 clear), which sit at their gps position rather than a
    marker slot.
]]]
attr[seg000:6737]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:673d]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:6757]: type = code; name = map_spawn_troop_icon; fn = in id: u8 @al, out carry: bool @cf; comment = [[[
    Spawn one troop icon: resolve the troop (al = id), bail unless it is
    visible/known (troop_0686e, troop_06770, bp >= 1), then create the icon
    (troop_icon_spawn_with_anim). CF clear on success.
]]]
attr[seg000:676e]: type = code
attr[seg000:6770]: type = code; name = troop_icon_pick_script; fn = in troop: *Troop @si, out carry: bool @cf; comment = [[[
    Pick the troops icon script (out bp = the script, 0 = no icon). Scripts are
    3-byte (sprite, dx, dy) steps, sprite 0 terminating; byte 0 is the initial
    sprite. bitfield_10 bit 4 hides the troop. Occupation bit 7 (with
    bitfield_10 bit 7 clear): script 181f only when the location status has bit
    4. Occupation bit 6 -> troop_icon_pick_script_moving. Occupation bits 4-5
    set: troop_icon_scripts_specialized[occ & 0xf], with occ & 0xf == 0 routed
    by equipment bits 6-7 (1813/1817/181b). Otherwise
    troop_icon_scripts_basic[occ & 0xf] (occ 0 with equipment bits 6-7 ->
    17bc/17c9/1806); script 1732 swaps to 16aa when the location status has bit
    1, and scripts 1774/1732 step +10 per position band ((position-1) & 7:
    <3 / 3 / 4 / >4 -> +0/+10/+20/+30).
]]]
attr[seg000:678a]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:67b3]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:67ba]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:67c1]: ofs_seg = seg001
