attr[seg000:6a87]: type = code; name = menu_callback_choice_troop_occupation_specialize_in_ecology
attr[seg000:6a89]: name = troop_apply_occupation_choice; comment = [[[
    The shared tail of the occupation verbs: apply cl as the new occupation
    (troop_06acb), let the troop react to it (arm_dialogue_interrupt_gate + a
    dialogue line with pending_room_action 0x0a, loc_07bb9) and take the change
    back if it refuses - a line whose event clears the gate. The refusal restores
    the pushed speech word and re-applies the pushed occupation BYTE (so bits
    0x10..0x80 come back too). On acceptance a troop that left the spice class
    hands its harvester back (equipment bit 7). Ends in menu_callback_choice_exit_menu.
]]]
attr[seg000:6a8c]: let = troop: *Troop @si
attr[seg000:6ac5]: name = troop_06ac5; fn = in troop: *Troop @si, in param_1: u8 @cl
attr[seg000:6acb]: name = troop_set_occupation; fn = in troop: *Troop @si, in param_1: u8 @cl; comment = [[[
    Give the troop (si) occupation cl: no-op when the nibble already matches.
    Assigning ecology (8) at location seg001:07c8 while it holds no bulbs becomes
    bulb growing (0x0a). Stores the whole byte, clears speech bits 4-5 and
    bitfield_10 bit 8, re-derives that bit from
    troop_call_callback_according_to_occupation (viability), refreshes the map icon
    (troop_08461), restarts the occupation clocks (06b25) and - for every
    occupation but 2 - marks the class in the speech word (0x2000 << class).
    Refreshes the order menu greys when this is the contacted troop.
]]]
attr[seg000:6ad4]: name = troop_06ad4; fn = in troop: *Troop @si, in param_1: u8 @cl
attr[seg000:6ad7]: let = location: *Location @di
attr[seg000:6b25]: name = troop_set_timePeriodOfRalliement_clear_troop_occupation_dependent_fields_06b25
attr[seg000:6b34]: type = code; name = troop_icon_anim_task; comment = [[[
    The troop icon animation task (interval 15, armed by
    callback_transition_05a56): steps each armed icons anim script (3-byte
    steps: sprite, dx, dy; sprite 0 loops to the scripts base unless flag bit 1)
    and moves + repaints it (troop_icon_move_and_redraw). Every 4th firing steps
    all icons, the rest only the focused one (troop_icon_focused_ptr).
]]]
attr[seg000:6b4b]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:6b8a]: type = code; name = troop_location_test_for_location_area_prospected; fn = in troop: *Troop @si, in location: *Location @di
attr[seg000:6b96]: type = code; name = troop_location_test_spice_mining_viable; fn = in troop: *Troop @si, in location: *Location @di; comment = [[[
    Can this troop mine spice here? Not with a damaged harvester (bitfield_10 bit
    9), a sulking troop (speech bits 4-5), spice_density < 1, or an area that is
    not prospected-and-unexhausted ((status ^ 0x40) & 0x41 != 0). Carry set = not
    viable; falls into troop_sync_occupation_stopped_bit.
]]]
attr[seg000:6bb6]: name = troop_sync_occupation_stopped_bit; comment = [[[
    The shared tail of the occupation viability tests: sync occupation bit 0x10 -
    the stopped-working bit the icon script reads - with the incoming carry (set =
    not viable). A flip refreshes the map icon, and the working-again direction
    also restarts the occupation clocks. pushf/popf keeps the carry, so the caller
    still reads the viability answer.
]]]
attr[seg000:6bd7]: type = code; name = troop_location_test_irrigation_viable; fn = in troop: *Troop @si, in location: *Location @di; comment = [[[
    Can this troop irrigate here? Not with a sulking troop (speech bits 4-5),
    water < 1, location status bit 5 clear, or without the troop own bulb
    equipment (mask 2). Carry set = not viable; falls into
    troop_sync_occupation_stopped_bit.
]]]
attr[seg000:6bf5]: type = [ofs16(seg000); 16]; name = array_callbacks_for_troop_occupation_06bf5
attr[seg000:6c15]: type = code; name = troop_call_callback_according_to_occupation
attr[seg000:6c21]: targets = seg000:0f66, seg000:6b8a, seg000:6b96, seg000:6bd7
attr[seg000:6c26]: type = [ofs16(seg000); 16]; name = array_callbacks_for_troop_occupation_06c26
attr[seg000:6c6f]: name = run_troop_occupation_events; comment = [[[
    The per-time-period walk over every troop (indices 0..66 - troops[67] is the
    terminator): skip a troop with speech bits 0x430 (-> the 6cd3 vegetation /
    moving branch), fold in one under 20 strong (troop_06d19), skip captured or
    unrallied ones (occupation & 0xa0), take a travel step for a moving one
    (occupation & 0x40 -> troop_08308), else call the occupation callback from
    array_callbacks_for_troop_occupation_06c26 with si = troop, di = its location,
    then age its skills (troop_usually_decrease_skills_every_4_days). Called from
    run_events_for_current_time_period (1b70).
]]]
