attr[seg000:6fe5]: type = code; name = callback_troop_location_for_troop_occupation_spice_mining; fn = in troop: *Troop @si, in location: *Location @di; comment = [[[
    One time period of spice mining. A damaged harvester (bitfield_10 bit 9) mines
    nothing until the daily repair slot comes round (the time period whose low
    nibble matches the troop id, 705c). Otherwise: the viability test, the worm /
    saboteur events (714c), then bitfield_10 bit 8 (working) and the accumulation -
    troop_0708a gives this period harvest, field_E accumulates it (every crossing
    of a 128 boundary raises the spice skill via troop_clamp_skill_and_do_something
    _else), one tenth of it goes to spice_in_stock with the remainder carried in
    data_046e1, and (harvest + location field_13) / location spice_amount is
    subtracted from spice_density with the remainder left in field_13. Eating past
    the overlay current shade bumps data_046ec so the spice-density overlay
    repaints. Not viable clears BOTH accumulators and stops the troop (loc_0707b).
]]]
attr[seg000:705c]: name = callback_troop_location_for_troop_occupation_spice_mining_harvester_was_previously_damaged
attr[seg000:7068]: comment = Damaged harvester is now fixed.
attr[seg000:7085]: type = code; name = callback_troop_make_troop_stop_working; fn = in troop: *Troop @si
attr[seg000:708a]: type = code; name = troop_update_harvest_rate; fn = in troop: *Troop @si; comment = [[[
    This time period spice harvest for the troop - the ACTUAL amount, not an
    estimate: seg000:6fff adds the return value to the troop running total, pays a
    tenth of it into spice_in_stock and takes the matching bite out of the location
    spice density. troop_prepare_troop_data_for_condit tail-jumps here (32c4) to
    stage the same number in ds:48, which the info panel shows as Current N kgs/h.
    
    (motivation modifier + spice skill high nibble) * population, quartered without
    a harvester (equipment bit 7), times ((location spice_density & 0xf0) + 1)
    taken from the product high byte, then byte-swapped, rolled left 1 and masked
    to 9 bits - which is the 16-bit product >> 7. The result replaces field_C and,
    when it changed, sets bitfield_10 bits 2-3 to 8 (it ROSE) or 4 (it fell).
]]]
