attr[seg000:780a]: name = map_open_troop_contact_menu; fn = in troop: *Troop @si; comment = [[[
    Open the contact verb menu over the troop (si), picking one of three menus:
    the full order menu (menu_map_troop_dialog) for a troop within
    location_visibility_distance that is standing still, the change-destination
    menu (menu_map_troop_moving_change_destination_next_troop) for a troop on the
    move (occupation bit 6), and the cycle menu
    (menu_map_troop_contact_cycle_troops) for one out of range or held prisoner
    (occupation bit 5, unless the freed-prisoner occupation 0x22). The order
    menu' last slot reads CUT CONTACT (0x53) while map_view_reentry_count is 0 and
    NO MORE ORDERS (0x52) once the room troop path re-entered the view. Staged
    with cleanup map_troop_contact_cleanup (loc_0d323).
]]]
attr[seg000:780d]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:7821]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:782a]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:783e]: ofs_seg = seg000
attr[seg000:7847]: name = map_setup_troop_dialog_menu; fn = in troop: *Troop @si; comment = [[[
    The order menu' grey bits (menu_map_troop_dialog): CHANGE TROOP OCCUPATION,
    MODIFY EQUIPMENT and MOVE TROOP all start greyed (0x40 in the text-id high
    byte). Dissatisfaction bit 0x400 leaves all three greyed. An occupation nibble
    other than 1 (spice prospecting) ungreys CHANGE TROOP OCCUPATION; nibble 2
    (awaiting orders) relabels it SELECT TROOP OCCUPATION (0x56) and returns.
    game_phase >= 5 ungreys MOVE TROOP. MODIFY EQUIPMENT needs game_phase >= 4, a
    non-repairing troop (bitfield_10 bit 0x200 clear), a location that allows
    handover (status bit 3, or appearance < 0x28) and some equipment on either
    side (the location_available_equipment counts or troop->equipment).
]]]
attr[seg000:78a3]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:78bc]: name = map_open_troop_info_popup; comment = [[[
    Open the troop info panel next to the troops icon (di): only within
    location_visibility_distance of the player (troop_distance_from_player);
    registers the troop in map_info_popup_troop_ptr, places + draws the panel
    (map_place_info_panel, height 100) and its content
    (map_draw_troop_info_panel_content).
]]]
attr[seg000:78d5]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:78e9]: name = map_draw_troop_info_panel_content; comment = [[[
    Draw the troop info panels content from the staged CONDIT block: the
    header string 0x3a (0x3b moving), the location name, the occupation and
    status lines (0x41/0x42, 0x3c, the skill caption at
    string_subst_id_table+12, 0x3d..0x43), then the Equipment header (0x6e) and
    the equipment icon row (draw_equipment_row). A troop that lost its icon
    closes the panel instead (map_close_troop_info_popup).
    The subst_id_04 bump at 78f7 moves the occupation caption that 0x3cs 0x84
    placeholder expands to from the 0x18.. dialogue wording to the 0x24.. panel
    wording ("Spice Mining", "Spice Prospecting", "Awaiting orders", ..).
]]]
attr[seg000:78fc]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:794f]: comment = {str_4h}\n{byte_3Ch}0 men  Motiv. {byte_36h}%
attr[seg000:79c4]: comment = "Equipment:"
attr[seg000:79d1]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:79de]: name = map_close_troop_info_popup; comment = [[[
    Close the troop info panel: clear map_info_popup_troop_ptr and
    map_popup_ptr, repaint the map beneath the panel rect and restore the
    comm-glow arrow overlay (loc_07b2b slot 8).
]]]
attr[seg000:79e8]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:79ee]: name = map_draw_troop_contact_popup; comment = [[[
    Draw the troop-contact dialogue popup (troop_contact_text_panel_record): a
    panel in the half of the screen the troop icon is NOT in (y0 = 5 when the icon
    sits at y >= 0x4c, else 0x50; height 0x43), with the head box (data_018f3, the
    panel origin + (4,3), 0x3d square, fill 0xe4 frame 0xf5) on the left and the
    subtitle descriptor seg001:2244 (origin panel + (0x49,3), 153x63, pads
    0/5/0/1) on the right. Sets data_046ef and map_popup_ptr. The head is 0x0c for
    an Atreides location (or status bit 1), else the generic Fremen 0x0f with the
    troop taken as fremen2_troop_ptrs[0]; its frame is drawn from data_022b9 into
    the head box inset one pixel (0x3b square). Also reached from
    subtitle_setup_layout (8cee) when a line is presented with no popup up.
]]]
attr[seg000:79f5]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:7a27]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:7a2a]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:7ac1]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:7b06]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:7b0f]: comment = [[[
    Open a map popup with vga effect al: clear the close-suppress flag (data_046d8),
    swap si<->di so ds:si = the animation source (icon/marker point) and es:di = the
    panel record, run the effect, then fall into the panel fill+frame (loc_07b1b).
    al=6 xor_rect_outline_advance from the info/location popups (seg000:5f76);
    al=2 xor_bracket_zoom_to_panel from the troop-contact popup (seg000:7a24).
]]]
attr[seg000:7b23]: targets = segvga:011e
attr[seg000:7b2b]: comment = [[[
    Close a map popup with vga effect al, unless data_046d8 suppresses it (set by
    map_select_troop when a new selection replaces the panel).
    al=8 xor_rect_outline_reverse from the info/location popups (seg000:5fad);
    al=4 xor_bracket_zoom_from_panel from the troop-contact popup (seg000:7b9f).
]]]
attr[seg000:7b36]: name = map_dismiss_troop_popups; comment = [[[
    Close any troop-contact UI over the map before a redraw: the no-more-orders teardown
    (menu_callback_choice_map_troop_contact_no_more_orders), the popup menu exit gated on
    data_046f8 (loc_05f79) and the troop marker overlay removal gated on data_046fa
    (loc_079de), bracketed by in_transition = 0x80.
]]]
attr[seg000:7b58]: name = map_close_troop_contact_popup; comment = [[[
    Tear down the troop-contact dialogue popup (data_046ef = the contacted
    troop): disable HUD element 18, stop the lip-sync, mark the contact
    (bitfield_10/12 masks + the contact day) unless already marked, repaint the
    popup panel rect (troop_contact_text_panel_record) and restore the overlay
    (loc_07b2b slot 4).
]]]
attr[seg000:7b8f]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:7ba3]: name = map_setup_troop_contact_popup; comment = [[[
    Put the contact popup up for the troop (si), unless data_046ef already names
    it - a further line only repaints the text. Latches data_046f1 (the troop
    subtitle_setup_layout rebuilds from), draws the popup
    (map_draw_troop_contact_popup) and runs the per-presentation setup (loc_09f40).
]]]
attr[seg000:7bb9]: name = troop_present_reaction_line; comment = [[[
    Present one dialogue line for the troop (si) with al staged in
    pending_room_action - the code the line conditions read to pick the reaction
    (0x0a = an occupation change). Stages the troop CONDIT block, latches
    data_046f1 (what subtitle_setup_layout rebuilds the popup from), resets
    dialogue_resume_entry_ptr and presents it as the Fremen-2 room person (0x0f),
    so on the map view it lands in the contact popup. Plays the voice on success
    and shares troop_07c02 tail (loc_07c56).
]]]
attr[seg000:7bc2]: comment = Store the caller-supplied action code (al) before presenting the troop dialogue line.
attr[seg000:7bed]: type = code; name = menu_callback_choice_map_troop_dialogue_ask_for_more_information; comment = [[[
    The order menu ASK FOR MORE INFORMATION verb: unless the equipment spinner
    panel is up (data_046f4 and data_046f5, -> loc_07e97), re-enter
    map_open_troop_contact_dialogue with the contacted troop (data_046ef) for its
    next line. Also the handler HUD element 18 carries while the popup is up, so a
    click on the text box does the same.
]]]
attr[seg000:7c02]: name = map_open_troop_contact_dialogue; comment = [[[
    The contacted troop' dialogue: (re)build the popup (map_setup_troop_contact_popup),
    stage the troop CONDIT block and the menu origin, then present one line into
    the popup (loc_09719) and play its voice (loc_09efd). Out of visibility range
    ds:4c = 0xff picks the record out-of-contact lines and the highlight ring
    swaps to the seg001:1916 script. The 7c2d loop retries once through the record
    head when the walk matched nothing. Interrupt gate 0x80 also brings up the
    equipment spinners (data_046f4 = 1, loc_07e1e).
]]]
attr[seg000:7c63]: name = troop_distance_from_player; comment = [[[
    The Chebyshev distance in map cells between the player and the troops gps
    position: max(|delta longitude| / the players lng_units_per_cell row,
    |delta latitude|). The troop twin of location_distance_from_player.
]]]
attr[seg000:7c8f]: name = location_distance_from_player; fn = in location: *Location @si; comment = [[[
