attr[seg000:9655]: name = npc_remove_companion_slot; fn = in npc: *RoomPerson @si; comment = [[[
    Remove the room-person from the companion HUD slots: person in ui_hud_companion_2 -> slot 2 = 0ffh; person in ui_hud_companion_1 -> shift slot 2 down into slot 1 (xchg leaves slot 2 = 0ffh); not a companion -> ret.
    Clears the vacated slot's blink counter (ui_hud_companion_blink[di-1152h] = 0) and redraws via ui_hud_draw_companions.
    Called from the travel-departure detach scan (seg000:40f5) and the dialogue-menu cleanup (loc_0982e) for a non-travelling speaker.
]]]
attr[seg000:9658]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:9673]: name = npc_assign_companion_slot; fn = in npc: *RoomPerson @si; comment = [[[
    Assign the room-person to a companion HUD slot: already in a slot -> ret; else the first empty (0ffh) of ui_hud_companion_1/2.
    Both full -> evict slot 1: encode the evicted person into pending_room_action (64h + person_index, the loc_09898 leave-scan lets them speak), npc_clear_travelling on their room_persons entry, shift slot 2 down, and store the newcomer in slot 2.
    The filled slot's blink counter is armed (ui_hud_companion_blink[di-1152h] = 10h -> 8 blinks) and ui_hud_draw_companions redraws.
    Reached from menu_npc_actions_cleanup (982b/9855) when the dialogue closes on a speaker with flags bit 40h (COME WITH ME).
]]]
