attr[seg000:9ab4]: name = head_sign_tick; comment = [[[
    The idle animator sign hook, run when a calm window budget is spent. Two steps
    one tick apart: with data_047e1 bit 7 clear, set it, prepare the digits
    (loc_09b09) and switch the head to the animation data_047e2 names with a
    20-frame window (data_047ce = 0x14), returning carry so the caller plays it
    instead of picking a calm animation; on the next tick (state 0x81) draw the
    row string interpolated at its x/y in its colour with the small font, present
    the game area, and return carry clear.
]]]
attr[seg000:9b49]: name = head_sign_lower; comment = [[[
    Take the speaker sign back down, called by the talk verb (949f) before the next
    line is presented. Only a raised sign carrying its number (data_047e1 == 0x80)
    lowers: play the animation AFTER the one that raised it (data_047e2 + 2 = the
    matching lowering), with data_047e1 = 0x81 so neither redraw clamp at 9c79/9ca6
    applies while it plays, pumping the frame tasks 12 ticks per frame
    (wait_processing_frame_tasks_interruptable with loc_099f6 as the advance) until
    the animation terminator. Then data_047e1 = 0. Any other state just clears it.
]]]
