attr[seg000:9d6a]: name = draw_talking_head_in_box; comment = [[[
    Draw one talking-head frame into the troop-contact popup head box: walk the
    frame image-group id list at si (0 ends it, 1 escapes to a 16-bit id),
    resolving each through the image-group table [47cc] and drawing it with
    draw_head_image_group_in_box. es = the screen buffer (the popup is painted
    there, not in fb1). The caller (map_draw_troop_contact_popup 7ac1) picks the
    animation - 0 for the HARK head, talking_head_idle_expr-1 for a Fremen one -
    and stages data_046d2/046d4 (the anchor) and data_047d4 (the box).
]]]
attr[seg000:9d94]: name = draw_head_image_group_in_box; comment = [[[
    Draw one image group re-anchored into the popup head box: each (sprite, x, y)
    lands at xy + ui_hud_elements[19] (the head rect origin) - data_046d2/046d4
    (the per-head anchor from talking_head_popup_anchor_table) + data_047d4 (the
    box origin), clipped to data_047d4. That shift is what frames heads of
    different sizes identically in the 0x3b box.
]]]
attr[seg000:9dda]: targets = segvga:0112
attr[seg000:9de3]: comment = [[[
    Speech mouth draw: stamp ONLY the lip-id frame over the live fb1, CLIPPED to the head mouth box ([current_head_mouth_box] + the element-19 origin, 9df8..9e0f).
    Each lip group bundles the torso/collar sprite under the mouth sprite; the clip confines that collar redraw to the mouth box (it erases the previous stamp overhang) and keeps it off the collar/ear stack elsewhere.
    No backdrop restore and no [239F0] diff-list update.
    The idle frame task keeps running during the voice (its callback at 99da never tests is_voc_pcm_playing); its calm-window redraws own the rest of the face, clamped above the mouth box (9c90).
]]]
attr[seg000:9df8]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:9e16]: comment = [[[
    Bank the lip-frame index by styling variant: frame = mouth + (facing-1)*4.
    facing 0 (the named heads) uses the mouth value directly (the js below).
    Each variant group is four mouth-region sprites drawn in that variant styling (FRM chiefs: beard/mouth; Paul: age); FRM1 lip anim = 60 frames = 15 variants x 4.
    The SMUG head (talking_head_id 0dh) adds one more per variant - a stride of 5.
]]]
attr[seg000:9e36]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:9e4b]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:9e57]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:9e64]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:9e75]: name = lip_sync_stamp_troop_popup; comment = [[[
    The speech mouth stamp while the full-map view owns the screen (the
    data_046eb sign branch at 9df1): the same lip-id frame select as the room path
    (mouth + (talking_head_idle_expr-1)*4, skipped for the HARK head 0x0c) but
    drawn re-anchored into the popup head box (draw_head_image_group_in_box).
    A multi-image lip group goes to fb1 and is presented over the box; a
    single-image one is drawn straight into the screen buffer.
]]]
