attr[seg000:a25b]: type = code; name = callback_event_dialogue_line_0a_hold_up_sign; comment = [[[
    Dialogue event 0x0a: the spoken line wants the speaker to hold up a sign with a
    number on it. Scan the seg001:1984 table (10-byte rows {phrase_id, string_id,
    x, y, colour}, sorted by phrase id) for current_subtitle_id; on a match arm
    data_047e1 = (state 1, animation index*2 0x0a - or 0x10 when the string id is
    exactly 0x38 - plus (talking_head_idle_expr-1)*4+2 for a banked head) and
    data_047e4 = the matched row. loc_09ab4, in the idle animator, then raises the
    sign and draws the row string at its position.
    
    The string ids are the "{word_XXh}0 kgs" templates: 0x30 = spice_in_stock
    (Duncan current stocks), 0x31/0x32 = yesterday production with the day-on-day
    gain/loss, 0x33..0x36 = the four negotiation figures, 0x37 = the demanded
    shipment. Ids >= 0x38 draw no text - those rows put digit sprites on the sign
    via loc_09b09 instead.
]]]
