attr[seg000:aca6]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:acae]: name = music_cd_start_selected_order; comment = [[[
    Shared tail of the STANDARD ORDER / SHUFFLE choices: stop the current song
    (midi_reset), pop the CD-order submenu and redraw the menu beneath, close the
    mixer panel (menu_callback_choice_exit_menu), clear the music-off bit
    (cmd_args_memory bit 4) and start the playlist (music_cd_playlist_restart).
]]]
attr[seg000:acbe]: type = code
attr[seg000:acbf]: name = music_cd_playlist_shuffle; ofs_seg = seg001; comment = [[[
    Shuffle the 9-entry CD playlist in place: 0x12 rounds of swapping two
    rand_iterated(8) slots, perturbing the rand seed with the PIT counter xor the
    loop counter between the two draws. Returns si = the playlist base.
]]]
attr[seg000:ace6]: name = music_cd_playlist_service; comment = [[[
    CD-playlist music streamer, stepped from process_frame_tasks (seg000:d9d2) and
    the in-game HNM play loop (seg000:c913). No-op while a VOC voice plays. In CD
    mode (music_playlist_flags bit 0) with the sky not suppressed and the driver
    idle: stamp the first idle sighting in music_song_end_tick_stamp, and 0xc8
    ticks later advance the playlist (music_cd_playlist_advance). In game-relative
    mode falls to loc_0ad37 (start the desired song when idle).
]]]
attr[seg000:ad18]: name = music_cd_playlist_advance; comment = [[[
    Advance the CD playlist: read the song at [music_cd_playlist_cursor]; a
    high-bit terminator restarts the playlist (music_cd_playlist_restart),
    otherwise bump the cursor and play the song.
]]]
attr[seg000:ad21]: name = music_cd_playlist_restart; ofs_seg = seg001; comment = [[[
    Restart the CD playlist from the top: in shuffle mode (music_playlist_flags
    bit 1) first permute the 9 entries (music_cd_playlist_shuffle), then set the
    cursor past the first entry and play it.
]]]
attr[seg000:ad37]: comment = [[[
    The game-relative per-frame music pump (reached from music_cd_playlist_service
    when the CD playlist is off, i.e. stepped by process_frame_tasks every frame):
    start the queued song (data_0dbcc) only when the driver is FULLY idle (status
    sign bit clear). Unlike service_midi_music (seg000:ae04) it does NOT treat a
    dynamics ramp (status bit 0x40) as a switch signal - every ramp raises 0x40
    (ADLSetDynamicsCurve), including the narration ducks and their end-of-line
    volume restores, so a 0x40 switch on this every-frame path would restart the
    playing song after each voice line.
]]]
attr[seg000:ad50]: type = code; name = play_music_WORMSUIT_HSQ
attr[seg000:ad57]: type = code; name = play_music_MORNING_HSQ
attr[seg000:ad5c]: comment = MORNING.HSQ
attr[seg000:ad95]: type = code; name = midi_play_song
attr[seg000:adbe]: name = midi_begin_song_fade_out; comment = [[[
    Begin the switch to the queued song (data_0dbcc): unless music is disabled, the
    CD playlist owns the driver, or a dynamics ramp is already running (status bit
    0x40), call MIDI_SetDynamics(ax = 0x12c ticks, bx = volume 0) to fade the
    current song out. The driver raises status bit 0x40 while the ramp runs and
    goes fully idle (status 0) when the fade reaches silence; service_midi_music
    starts data_0dbcc on either condition (seg000:ae10/ae17) - during a travel
    confirm that is the first orni takeoff frame, giving the audible music stop
    between the room theme and the flight theme.
]]]
attr[seg000:ade0]: name = midi_duck_music_volume; comment = [[[
    Drop the MIDI music to its narration "duck" level via MIDI_SetDynamics.
    ax = 0x64 (ramp duration in ticks).
    bl = data_0289e (target volume, clamped to >= 4 in the shared tail at loc_0adf8).
    bh = data_028b6.
    Falls into loc_0adf8 which calls [MIDI_SetDynamics] vtable.
    Called by play_intro2_cutscenes (seg000:0238) before each narration clip, plus other in-game spots where voice playback temporarily ducks the score.
]]]
attr[seg000:aded]: name = midi_restore_music_volume; comment = [[[
    Ramp the MIDI music back to its normal level via MIDI_SetDynamics, symmetric to midi_duck_music_volume.
    ax = 0x190 (ramp duration in ticks - longer than the duck so the music swells back gently).
    bl = data_02896.
    bh = data_028ae.
    Falls into the shared loc_0adf8 tail (clamp bl >= 4, then call [MIDI_SetDynamics]).
    Called by play_intro2_cutscenes (seg000:0257) after each narration clip ends, plus the room-screen voice cleanup paths.
]]]
attr[seg000:ae04]: name = service_midi_music; comment = [[[
    Service MIDI music playback: bail when music is disabled (loc_0aec6) or the CD
    playlist owns the driver (music_playlist_flags bit 0); advance into the queued
    song (loc_0ad43) when the driver is idle (status sign clear) OR a dynamics ramp
    is running (status bit 0x40) - the mid-ramp switch that completes a
    midi_begin_song_fade_out. Deliberately NOT called from the game loop: the
    per-frame pump is loc_0ad37, idle-only, because 0x40 also rides the narration
    duck/restore ramps. Callers are the room-screen presents (18ae/2e47), the orni
    takeoff/landing loops (4816/4927), the globe view (5a53) and the mixer paths
    (aefd/b8de).
]]]
attr[seg000:ae2f]: type = code; name = check_pcm_enabled
attr[seg000:ae44]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:ae59]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:ae62]: type = code; name = midi_load_song
attr[seg000:aeaf]: type = code; name = menu_callback_choice_music_off
attr[seg000:aeb7]: type = code; name = midi_reset; comment = [[[
    Stop the currently playing song.
    Clears [_byte_2D07B_current_song_index] to 0 and calls the driver-supplied MIDI_Reset (ADLReset for DNADL: silences all OPL voices and clears the driver status byte). The driver returns 0 in al, which is stored in [_byte_2D07D_midi_status], disabling subsequent midi_wait_until calls.
    Called before each play_music_* (to silence the previous song) and again from per-stage play loops like play_VIRGIN_HNM once the music reaches a target measure (one-shot termination — the song-index check prevents it from re-firing).
]]]
attr[seg000:aec6]: name = check_music_enabled; comment = [[[
    Music service gate: returns CF set (music disabled) when cmd_args_memory bit 4
    (the MUSIC OFF menu toggle) is set or the settings MIDI flag (settings_flags
    bit 0x100, loc_0ae28) is clear.
]]]
attr[seg000:aed6]: type = code; name = callback_main_ui_element_03; comment = [[[
    THE BOOK hud verb: open the diary screen. Only outside other modes
    (game_screen_mode_flags == 0): tear down the room view, fold the hud head,
    set the book flags to 1, suspend the game clock, select the room ui table,
    service music, then transition 0x34 into callback_transition_0af26.
]]]
attr[seg000:aef7]: ofs_seg = seg000
attr[seg000:af00]: type = code; name = book_menu_update_topic_availability; comment = [[[
    Grey out empty book topics: for each of the three topic menu entries (paul-
    on-dune/spice/fremen) probe the dialogue-played log for a page carrying that
    topic (book_find_first_page with bh=4/8/0xc); set menu-id bit 0x4000
    (disabled) when none exists, clear it otherwise.
]]]
attr[seg000:af12]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:af26]: type = code; name = callback_transition_0af26; comment = [[[
    Book-open transition body: switch the frieze to the open-book sides,
    install the six book controls (ui_globe_rotation_controls[6..11]: dead
    slot, prev/next arrows, close hotspots) over hud elements 12..17, grey out
    empty topics, reset the topic filter, push menu_book on the screen-element
    stack, and fall into the cover draw.
]]]
attr[seg000:af29]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:af38]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:af3b]: ofs_seg = seg000
attr[seg000:af43]: type = code; name = callback_transition_0af43; comment = [[[
    Draw the book cover: set book flags bit 1 (at cover), clear the game area,
    draw BOOK.HSQ sprite 0, hide hud element 23, draw the hud head.
]]]
attr[seg000:af58]: type = code; name = menu_callback_choice_book_all_topics
attr[seg000:af60]: type = code; name = menu_callback_choice_book_paul_on_dune_topic
attr[seg000:af68]: type = code; name = menu_callback_choice_book_spice_topic
attr[seg000:af70]: type = code; name = menu_callback_choice_book_fremen_topic
attr[seg000:af76]: name = book_topic_select_common; comment = [[[
    Common tail of the four topic menu verbs (bx = topic filter, bp = entry
    offset). If a page is showing (bit 1 of the book flags clear) first flip
    back to the cover (book_turn_back_to_cover). Find the first matching page;
    if none, do nothing. Otherwise store the topic filter, reset the bookmark
    to the log start, move the 0x8000 highlight to the chosen menu entry, and
    fall into the next-page callback to show the first match.
]]]
attr[seg000:afa0]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:afb5]: type = code; name = callback_ui_element_book_next_page; comment = [[[
    Book next-page arrow (and shared tail of the topic verbs). Search forward
    (dx=2) from the bookmark; from the cover (flags bit 1) search starts at the
    bookmark itself (dx=0). On a hit: bookmark it, run the page-turn animation,
    play SN2.VOC and transition 0x0e into book_draw_current_page. Past the last
    page: start the scrolling CREDITS.HNM (flags bit 2 latches it, once).
]]]
attr[seg000:afc7]: type = code; name = callback_ui_element_book_prev_page; comment = [[[
    Book previous-page arrow. Ignored on the cover (flags bit 1). If the
    credits are rolling (flags bit 2): undo the past-end step (bookmark += 2),
    remove the credits frame task and restart normal music service. Then search
    backward (dx=-2); running off the front flips back to the cover.
]]]
attr[seg000:affa]: ofs_seg = seg000
attr[seg000:b01e]: ofs_seg = seg000
attr[seg000:b024]: name = book_turn_back_to_cover; comment = [[[
    Flip the book back to its cover: backward page-turn animation (dh=0xff),
    then SN2.VOC + transition 0x0e into callback_transition_0af43 (redraw the
    cover and set flags bit 1).
]]]
attr[seg000:b029]: ofs_seg = seg000
attr[seg000:b02c]: name = book_page_turn_present; comment = [[[
    Present a page turn: stop any VOC, play SN2.VOC (papers ruffle) and run
    transition 0x0e with the draw callback already in bp.
]]]
attr[seg000:b031]: comment = Play SN2.VOC - Papers ruffle
attr[seg000:b039]: type = code; name = book_draw_current_page; comment = [[[
    Draw the bookmarked page. Clear book flags bits 1-2, then build the page
    text at data_0a6b0: speaker-attribution phrase (0xf3 + page-word bits 11..15,
    the lip-sync id logged with the line, e.g. "And the Duke said to Paul:")
    followed by the sentence phrase (bank 8 | record bits), 0xff-terminated, and
    render it via draw_subtitle_text_from_si (book layout + drop cap).
    Also: look up a page video (book_lookup_page_video), draw the page border
    rect (data_02408), the hud head, the sprite-4 flourish from BOOK.HSQ when
    the text ends above y=138, the topic tag (phrase 0x103 + record flag bits
    2-3: " "/Paul Atreides/Spice/The Fremen) on every page but the first, and
    the two-digit page number at (306,3). Pages with a video get hud element 23
    armed (flags 0x80) and three camera icons (sprite = video id - 11) drawn
    down the left edge.
]]]
attr[seg000:b03e]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:b08b]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:b0ac]: comment = RES_BOOK_HSQ
attr[seg000:b0d1]: comment = Topic tag: 0x103 " " / 0x104 "Paul Atreides" / 0x105 "Spice" / 0x106 "The Fremen"
attr[seg000:b114]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:b126]: name = book_append_phrase_to_text; comment = [[[
    Append phrase ax to the subtitle text buffer at the data_047bc cursor
