    dec game_suspend_count, clamped at 0 (falls into suspend_game_clock to re-inc
    when it would go negative) — resume one suspend level.
]]]
attr[seg000:b2b9]: name = suspend_game_clock; comment = inc game_suspend_count — suspend the in-game clock and idle events one level.
attr[seg000:b2be]: name = reset_game_suspend; comment = [[[
    Zero game_suspend_count, fully resuming the in-game clock and idle animations.
    Called from start (seg000:0034, begin gameplay) and after scene/menu
    transitions (0ebe/0f9c/0fde/loc_01755/b3fd).
]]]
attr[seg000:b30f]: type = code; name = load_save_game_timestamp; ofs_seg = seg001; comment = [[[
    For each save slot (digit 31h.. patched into dune37s0.sav[7]), open the file
    and read its first word - the game_time stamped by create_save_cl - into the
    scratch at ds:0d816h, then format it into the load-menu entry via loc_0b2c4.
    Menu-entry words at [si] get their top 2 bits set from the file-exists result;
    si advances 4 per slot until the 0a3h sentinel ends the menu.
]]]
attr[seg000:b35a]: type = code; name = menu_callback_choice_globe_save_game
attr[seg000:b379]: comment = "SAVE ERROR"
attr[seg000:b389]: type = code; name = create_save_cl; comment = [[[
    Save the game to slot cl: patch the slot digit (31h+cl) into the dune37s0.sav
    template, build the save image (create_save_in_memory), stamp game_time as a
    u16 file header at es:0, RLE-compress the image to es:2 (compress_sav), then
    create the file and write header+compressed block (cx+2 bytes) via loc_0f27c.
    CF set on DOS file error (caller shows SAVE ERROR).
]]]
attr[seg000:b3b0]: type = code; name = menu_callback_choice_globe_load_game; comment = [[[
    Load the game from slot cl: patch the slot digit into dune37s0.sav, read the
    whole file into a fresh scratch segment, move the compressed block (file
    bytes 2..end, skipping the u16 game_time header) up against offset 0x5779,
    decompress_sav back down to es:0, and restore_from_save_memory. The current
    room_view_toggle is preserved across the load (saved value discarded), frame
    tasks are cleared, and the room or globe screen is rebuilt to match.
]]]
attr[seg000:b3c7]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:b3d9]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:b427]: type = code; name = create_save_in_memory; comment = [[[
    Build the uncompressed 0x567a-byte save image in a fresh 0x578-paragraph
    scratch segment at es:100h. Four regions, back to back:
      +0000 (0x317f bytes): map overlay bits - bits 5-4 (mask 30h) of each of the
             0xc5fc map cells at [_word_2D1AE_res_map_ofs], packed 4 cells/byte,
             first cell in bits 7-6.
      +317f (0xa2 bytes): the dialogue-played log at cs:0aah..14bh (see
             dialogue_played_log_head).
      +3221 (0x11f8 bytes): the DIALOGUE buffer at ds:0aa76h (per-line spoken/event
             flag bits are the mutable part; relocated sub-resource pointers ride along).
      +4419 (0x1261 bytes): the game-state block ds:0000..1260h (globals, locations,
             troops, room_persons, smugglers, travel/UI tail).
    Returns es:di = image at es:100h, cx = 0x567a.
]]]
attr[seg000:b454]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:b45d]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:b473]: type = code; name = restore_from_save_memory; comment = [[[
    Inverse of create_save_in_memory: scatter a decompressed save image at ds:si
    back into live memory. Unpacks the 0x317f packed map bytes into bits 5-4 of
    the 0xc5fc map cells at [ss:0dd00h]:0 (merge mask: cell = cell & 0cfh | bits),
    then copies 0xa2 bytes to the dialogue-played log at cs:0aah, 0x11f8 bytes to
    the DIALOGUE buffer at ss:0aa76h, and 0x1261 bytes to the game-state block at
    ss:0000.
]]]
attr[seg000:b4aa]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:b4bb]: type = code; name = decompress_sav; comment = [[[
    Byte-RLE decompressor for save games (inverse of compress_sav). In: ds:si =
    compressed block, es:di = output. Reads the u16 escape value (low byte) and
    u16 block length, then copies literals until the escape byte introduces a
    (count, value) run. Returns cx = decompressed length, di = entry di.
]]]
attr[seg000:b4bc]: comment = Read RLE control byte
attr[seg000:b4bf]: comment = Read input size
attr[seg000:b4ea]: type = code; name = compress_sav; comment = [[[
    Byte-RLE compressor for save games. In: ds:si = source, es:di = output slot,
    cx = source length. Output block: u16 escape value (dl = 0f7h; dh is leftover
    run-counter garbage, decoder reads the low byte only), u16 block length
    (4 + stream bytes, header included), then the stream. Stream: run of 3..255
    equal bytes, or any run of the escape byte, emits (escape, count, value);
    runs of 1-2 other bytes emit the bytes literally. A 0000h terminator word is
    stored after the stream but excluded from the length and never written to disk.
    Returns cx = block length.
]]]
attr[seg000:b527]: comment = Write RLE-byte (in word)
attr[seg000:b52a]: comment = Write output length
attr[seg000:b532]: name = read_map_byte_at_dx_bl; comment = [[[
    Read the MAP.HSQ terrain byte at longitude dx / latitude bl (via map_func;
    dx is preserved). Bit 0x40 = a location is at this cell (set by the startup
    loop at seg000:0192).
]]]
attr[seg000:b56c]: name = map_build_cell_strip; comment = [[[
    Build a rows x cols block of the planet map centred on (x = longitude,
    lat = latitude row) into the data_09e68 scratch of 3-byte [map byte, map
    offset] entries, row-major. Latitude centred at lat - rows/2, clamped to the
    south pole; each row is a horizontal run of cols cells centred on the
    longitude cell, wrapping within the row.
]]]
attr[seg000:b57b]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:b586]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:b58b]: type = code; name = map_func
attr[seg000:b5a0]: type = code; name = tablat_lookup_from_bx_to_ax_bp
attr[seg000:b5c5]: name = map_offset_and_snap_x; comment = [[[
    map_func wrapper used by the startup location loop (seg000:0192): es:di = the
    map byte for (dx = longitude, bx = latitude), and dx is snapped to the start
    of its map cell (dx = row_byte_offset * 0x10000 / (2 * tablat_len)), so a
    location's stored map_x compares equal (loc_04002) when a desert walk lands
    on its cell.
]]]
attr[seg000:b5cf]: name = desert_apply_step_delta; comment = [[[
    Apply a desert_step_deltas word (ax) to the desert position: dx = longitude
    (0..0xffff around the planet), bl = signed latitude row (-97..97), bh = the
    fine sub-row position (0..255 between latitude rows). ah steps bh, carrying
    into bl clamped to bl < 0x62 going south and bl > -0x62 (0x9e) going north
    (a blocked step is undone); al (sign-extended) is added to dx.
]]]
attr[seg000:b5f9]: name = map_screen_to_position; fn = in x: u16 @dx, in y: u16 @bx, out map_x: u16 @dx, out lat: u16 @bx; comment = [[[
    The inverse of map_position_to_screen: convert a screen point inside the
    map window to a map position. Subtract the window centre
    (data_0dcf6/data_0dcf8), add the view latitude for the row; the longitude
    cell = the screen dx plus the rows cached view-centre cell (the tablat
    entry +6 scratch map_copy_window_row fills), wrapped into the row length
    ([si+2] * 2), then scaled back to longitude units (cell * 0x10000 / len).
    On the full globe (data_046eb bit 0x80) both deltas are unscaled by 4 and
    the +4 rotated-band offset applies instead.
]]]
attr[seg000:b61e]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:b647]: name = map_position_to_screen; comment = [[[
    Project a map position (dx = longitude units, bx = latitude) to map-view
    screen coordinates. y = (lat - zoomed_globe_latitude) + window centre
    (data_0dcf8); x = window centre (data_0dcf6) + high word of
    (lng - zoomed_globe_longitude) * the latitudes tablat row byte length
    (the same lng * len >> 16 cell projection map_copy_window_row uses).
    Globe mode (data_046eb bit 0x80) scales both deltas by 4.
]]]
attr[seg000:b6c3]: type = code; name = map_draw_zoomed_globe; comment = [[[
    Draw the map main view. Globe mode (data_046eb bit 0x80): centre (0xa0,0x4c),
    clamp latitude to +-0x4b and call vga_draw_map_zoomed (the full interpolated
    globe). Windowed mode: derive centre/size from data_046e3_rect into
    data_0dcf2..0dcf8, clamp latitude to +-(0x56 - height/2), copy one raw map row
    per window row into the ss row buffer (map_copy_window_row, walking tablat
    entries north of the centre mirrored/negated), and blit it with
    vga_blit_shaded (pixel = (cell & 0x0f) + 0x10, curved edges) unless data_046eb
    bit 0x40 suppresses the blit.
]]]
attr[seg000:b6f8]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:b708]: ofs_seg = seg001
