attr[seg000:b993]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:b9ae]: type = code; name = frame_task_callback_0b9ae; comment = [[[
    The globe rotation frame task (interval 1).
    Each tick: es = fb1; call vga_globe_setup - draw ONE globe outline row into fb1; return while the pass is unfinished (carry clear).
    On the carry return (pass complete): loc_0baf2 computes the player globe-cursor position (dx=0 while suppress_sky_240_255 is set, i.e. outside the in-game map),
    restore the mouse if it overlaps the sprite clip rect, present the clip rect fb1->screen (update_screen_at_sprite_rect_updating_head),
    redraw the globe cursor (dx!=0) and the mouse, then advance the rotation phase by 1 (ax=1, globe_rotation_increment_ax) for the next pass.
    A pass is 2*outline_rows+1 calls, so the globe creeps one phase step (1/398 revolution) per pass.
]]]
attr[seg000:b9b2]: targets = segvga:0148
attr[seg000:b9b9]: type = code; name = callback_ui_element_0b9b9
attr[seg000:b9c0]: type = code; name = callback_ui_element_0b9c0
attr[seg000:b9cc]: type = code; name = callback_ui_element_0b9cc
attr[seg000:b9d3]: type = code; name = callback_ui_element_0b9d3
attr[seg000:b9e0]: type = code; name = globe_rotation_increment_ax; ofs_seg = seg001; comment = [[[
    Advance the globe rotation phase by ax (signed): dx = [_dword_23DFC] + ax, wrapped into 0..0x18e (398 phase units = one revolution),
    then fall through into recalculate_globe_rotation_table to rebuild the per-row fp for the new phase.
]]]
attr[seg000:b9f6]: type = code; name = recalculate_globe_rotation_table; comment = [[[
    Rebuild the per-row rotation fixed-point in the in-memory TABLAT (entries {offset:u16, len:u16, fp:u32}, fp stored hi word first).
    Entry: si = _dword_23DFC (entry-0 fp) holding the seed, dx:ax = seed<<16 | 0x8000 still live from the ba78 mul.
    bx = (seed<<16 + 0x8000) / 398; for each of the 98 remaining rows: fp = 2 * bx * row len.
]]]
attr[seg000:ba15]: type = code; name = globe_increment_tilt_by_ax
attr[seg000:ba20]: comment = ax = min(ax + ds:word_21910, 98)
attr[seg000:ba28]: comment = ax = max(-98, ax)
attr[seg000:ba2d]: name = build_globe_tilt_window_table; comment = [[[
    Rebuild the 196-word tilt window table at globe_tilt_window_table from _word_21910_globe_tilt.
    Each word encodes a (section, latitude) pair: ah = 0 marks the southern sections, ah = 0xff (word-negative) the northern; al >= 0 near side, al < 0 the far (wrapped-past-the-pole) side.
    The south run starts at al = tilt + 98 and counts down to the window start, so the latitude visible at the fixed window centre (+0xc4) is (outline byte - tilt): the tilt carries the map-row sign (positive = south, negative = north).
    vga_globe_setup indexes the table from its middle by the GLOBDATA outline latitude byte (segvga:1d85) and dispatches its quadrant branches on the two sign channels.
]]]
attr[seg000:ba2f]: ofs_seg = seg001
attr[seg000:ba75]: type = code; name = set_globe_tilt_and_rotation; ofs_seg = seg001; comment = [[[
    Seed the globe orientation from dx = longitude, bx = latitude.
    Stores the rotation fixed-point seed: _dword_23DFC (the TABLAT entry-0 fp field) = hi word of 398 * dx, lo word 0.
    Clamps the tilt magnitude up to at least 0x20 (ba86..ba93, unsigned compares: 0..0x1f -> 0x20, -0x1f..-1 -> -0x20) and stores it in _word_21910_globe_tilt.
    Then rebuilds the per-row rotation fp table (recalculate_globe_rotation_table) and the tilt window table (loc_0ba2d).
]]]
attr[seg000:ba9e]: type = code; name = callback_ui_element_0ba9e
