    Read a 2-byte little-endian size word from the file into ax.
    The value lands at es:[si-2] in the read buffer after the read.
]]]
attr[seg000:cd97]: comment = Re-read it from the buffer: ax = size word just read.
attr[seg000:cda0]: type = code; name = hnm_open_at_body_start; comment = [[[
    Reset the buffers and load the first frame, placing the read buffer at the
    top of the framebuffer scratch area, then read that frame's bytes.
]]]
attr[seg000:cda8]: comment = Place the frame at the top of the scratch area: framebuffer_size - size - 2.
attr[seg000:cdb5]: comment = Store the size word at the head of the buffer.
attr[seg000:cdbc]: comment = [[[cx = frame size minus the 2 size bytes; fall through to read it.]]]
attr[seg000:cdbf]: type = code; name = hnm_read_bytes; comment = [[[
    Seek the HNM file handle to the current offset and read cx bytes into the
    read buffer, retrying on short reads; then advance the offset/remaining
    counters. Aborts (carry set) when no file is open.
]]]
attr[seg000:cdc3]: comment = No file open (handle < 1) -> return with carry set.
attr[seg000:cdc8]: comment = Seek to the current absolute file offset (INT 21h/42h).
attr[seg000:cdd7]: comment = Read cx bytes into the buffer at ds:dx (INT 21h/3Fh).
attr[seg000:cde1]: comment = Short read -> seek and retry from the top.
attr[seg000:cde5]: comment = Advance file_remaining down and file_offset up by the bytes read.
attr[seg000:cdf7]: type = code; name = hnm_advance_read_ptr; comment = Advance the buffer write cursor and the buffered-byte count by ax.
attr[seg000:ce01]: type = code; name = hnm_reset_frame_counter; comment = Zero the frame counter, then fall through to reset the timing counters.
attr[seg000:ce07]: type = code; name = hnm_reset_counters; comment = Reset the secondary HNM timing counters (counter_2 = 0, counter_3/4 = -1).
attr[seg000:ce1a]: type = code; name = hnm_reset_buffers; comment = [[[
    Point the read/decode buffers at the saved framebuffer segment, clear the
    cursors and the buffered-byte count, and reset the working size to the
    framebuffer size.
]]]
