attr[seg000:d280]: name = play_pending_panel_fold; comment = [[[
    When a verb-panel transition is pending (loc_0d316 armed in_transition to a
    small positive), reveal the fb1-staged command panel with the 17-frame
    accordion fold (loc_0c0d5 al=0x18 -> panel_anim_play_step, looped cx=0x11),
    interleaving lip_sync_frame_task so the talking head keeps moving, then clear
    in_transition. in_transition < 0 (0x80, a full-screen transition) or 0 = no-op.
]]]
attr[seg000:d285]: comment = <=0 (idle, or a full-screen transition handled elsewhere): nothing to fold, return.
attr[seg000:d287]: comment = preserve caller registers across the fold.
attr[seg000:d28a]: comment = consume the pending flag now so re-entry is a no-op.
attr[seg000:d28f]: comment = raise the HUD hands ornament before revealing the panel.
attr[seg000:d292]: comment = 17 accordion fold steps.
attr[seg000:d295]: comment = save the fold-step counter across the step body.
attr[seg000:d296]: comment = record the PIT tick at the start of this step for pacing.
attr[seg000:d29a]: comment = si = staged fb1 segment holding the new command panel.
attr[seg000:d29e]: comment = al = effect id 0x18 (accordion fold).
attr[seg000:d2a0]: comment = advance one fold step, blitting fb1 onto the visible screen.
attr[seg000:d2a3]: comment = bx = the step-start tick recorded above.
attr[seg000:d2a4]: comment = inner pacing loop: keep the talking head animating while waiting.
attr[seg000:d2a5]: comment = advance the lip-sync talking head one frame.
attr[seg000:d2a9]: comment = ax = current PIT tick.
attr[seg000:d2ac]: comment = ax = ticks elapsed since this fold step started.
attr[seg000:d2ae]: comment = pace each fold step to 6 PIT ticks.
attr[seg000:d2b1]: comment = spin on lip_sync_frame_task until 6 ticks have elapsed.
attr[seg000:d2b3]: comment = restore the fold-step counter.
attr[seg000:d2b4]: comment = next fold step.
attr[seg000:d2b6]: comment = lower the HUD hands ornament once the panel is fully revealed.
attr[seg000:d2b9]: comment = restore caller registers.
attr[seg000:d2bd]: name = dismiss_stacked_overlays; comment = [[[
    Before a view switch, tear down the transient menus/overlays stacked over the
    base room menu on the screen-element stack (data_021da), running each one's
    cleanup func via screen_element_stack_pop_and_cleanup (loc_0d2ea). The drain stops
    at a base/locked entry: leading priority byte 0xff (command_menu_buf / mirror
    overlay) or low nibble 0. in_transition (_byte_2D196) is forced to 0x80 across the
    loop so the cleanups' repaints do not arm a panel fold, then restored.
]]]
