attr[seg000:d445]: name = dispatch_command_menu_slot; comment = [[[
    Dispatch the active command-menu row cx: read its [text_id, handler] record via
    loc_0d454, and unless handler==0 or the greyed flag (text_id & 0x4000) is set,
    jmp to the handler. Entered from the five per-row ui_element click handlers
    d443/d43e/d439/d434/d42f (cx = 0..4).
]]]
attr[seg000:d454]: name = read_command_menu_record_for_slot; comment = [[[
    Read slot cx of the active screen elements command-record buffer (top of the
    screen-element stack, seg001:21da): skip the header byte, index the cx-th 4-byte
    [text_id, handler] record, and return ax=text_id (with flags) and bx=handler.
    When cx == data_0dce5 it returns the scroll "more" arrow handler instead.
]]]
attr[seg000:d48a]: name = draw_command_menu_item; comment = [[[
    Draw one verb-menu slot (cl = slot 0..4, ax = text_id with state bits) into ui_elements[7+cl].
    Pen x = 5dh, y = ui_elements[7+cl].y0 + 1, small font. text_id & 3fffh = the COMMAND/PHRASE id (0 = blank slot).
    Colour: 0fah enabled (sets flags bit 80h), 0f5h when bit 4000h set (disabled/greyed), fg/bg swapped when bit 8000h set (highlighted); default bg 0f3h.
    Draws a leading space + the resolved string, then fills the rest of the row (x..0e3h, y..y+7) with the bg colour.
]]]
