attr[seg000:e353]: type = code; name = wait_processing_frame_tasks_interruptable; comment = [[[
    Wait ax PIT ticks, having called bp ONCE up front. Whether it services frame
    tasks depends on suppress_sky_240_255 (data_0227d):
      != 0 (intro / cutscene state) - each spin calls any_key_pressed, which on the
        no-input path runs process_frame_tasks (dda6) and on input returns carry so
        the wait breaks early. Callers that want this bracket themselves with
        inc/dec suppress_sky_240_255 (0d4e/0d89, 1566/1579).
      == 0 (in-game, set at 029d) - only pause_if_p_key_pressed runs: a plain timed
        spin, no task servicing and no input break.
    head_sign_lower (9b75) is an in-game caller, so its per-frame pacing does NOT
    re-enter the idle animator - which matters, because that would re-enter
    head_sign_tick with data_047e1 at 0x81 and re-draw the sign text.
    Contrast wait_a_bit (e387), which calls process_frame_tasks itself (e3ae).
]]]
