attr[seg001:1225]: type = [LocationRoom; 12]; name = atreides_palace_rooms; comment = [[[
    Per-location scene descriptors for palace-category locations. Selected by
    draw_SAL via loc_03efe: [13c4 table][dh] picks this table for dh=0x20, and
    the dx low byte (dl) indexes it as palace_rooms[dl-1].
    
    `background` is the room byte consumed by draw_SAL (seg000:3b59):
    SAL room sub-chunk = (background - 1) & 0x0f
    sprite-sheet res   = ((background - 1) >> 4) + 0x13  (RES_GENERIC_HSQ + n)
    The SAL file itself is chosen separately from locations[bh-1].appearance via
    calc_SAL_index. e.g. the intro equipment room (dx=0x2002, dl=2) reads
    palace_rooms[1].background = 0x3a -> PALACE.SAL room 9 + RES_EQUI_HSQ.
    
    exits[0..3] are the four direction exits, indexed by compass direction:
    0 = UP/N, 1 = RIGHT/E, 2 = DOWN/S, 3 = LEFT/W (the same indices the
    bottom-right HUD compass buttons ui_elements[13..17] use). Encoding:
        0x00        no exit in this direction.
        0x01..0x7F  destination room number — ui_click_move_room (seg000:3f27)
                    stores it as the new location_and_room low byte at
                    seg000:3faa after the `js` non-special branch is not taken.
        0x80..0xFF  special-exit dispatch via the jump table at cs:1454h
                    (seg000:3fd2..3ff7). The 0xFB..0xFF subrange is what
                    rebuild_and_draw_room_nav_panel (seg000:305c) shows as a
                    visible HUD arrow; the rest are in-scene/scripted exits.
]]]
