attr[seg001:3cbe]: type = u16; name = troop_icon_count; comment = [[[
    Count of live records in troop_icons. The troop icon renderer is the games
    general "several layered sprites over a restored backdrop" engine: its main
    use is the troop icons on the full map view, and the night attack scene
    reuses it as a particle system (seg000:0b3e/0bbe).
]]]
attr[seg001:3cc0]: name = troop_icons; comment = [[[
    The troop icon list: 0x11-byte records, troop_icon_count entries.
    +0/+2 = the icons top-left screen x/y, +4/+6 = its bottom-right corner
    (from the sprite header), +8 = the ONMAP sprite id, +0xa = the owning
    troop ptr, +0xc = flags (bit 0 anim script armed, bit 1 no-loop, bit 6
    draw-last/protected, bit 7 hidden), +0xd = the anim script cursor and
    +0xf its base (3-byte steps: sprite, dx, dy). The night attack scene
    reuses the array as its particle pool.
]]]
