    6-byte entries [location ptr:u16, screen x:u16, screen y:u8, data_046eb
    copy:u8], terminated by a 0 word. The map hover tracker (loc_04586) resolves
    the cursor against it; map_screen_cleanup clears the head.
]]]
attr[seg001:aa6e]: type = u16
attr[seg001:aa72]: type = u16; name = _word_29F22_res_condit_ofs
attr[seg001:aa74]: type = u16; name = _word_29F24_res_condit_seg
attr[seg001:aa76]: type = [u8; 4496]; name = DIALOGUE; comment = [[[
    The DIALOGUE resource (index 0xbd) HSQ-decompressed in place into this fixed buffer (seg001:aa76-bc06) by initialize_resources2: di=0aa76h at seg000:011a, open_resource_force_hsq at seg000:0120 decompresses here. adjust_sub_resource_pointers (seg000:0123) then relocates the sub-resource offset table at the start of the buffer by adding the base 0aa76h.
    
    The sub-resources are the per-person dialogue records (8 slots each). Each 4-byte sentence entry is read big-endian as word0,word1 = bytes B0 B1 B2 B3:
    B0 flags/event: 0x0f event-callback id (a049); 0x10 set -> the .voc variant letters are random alternates (rand_masked(3) into the a8ff letter, 89dd), clear -> they are sequential multi-part takes (94e8 current_subtitle_id += 0x1000, one per 0xFE phrase segment); latched (8ac6); 0x20 auto-dialogue skip (9fba); 0x40 always-offer (9fb6); 0x80 spoken (a097).
    B1: condition id low 8 bits.
    B2: 0x03 phrase index bits 8..9; 0x0c replay-log eligibility (a05e); 0x10 voiced-line flag (a0f8); 0x20 unused/reserved; 0xc0 condition id bits 8..9.
    B3: phrase index low 8 bits.
    Records at or past dialogue_phrase12_first_record_ptr (buffer offset 0x60) read PHRASE12, earlier ones PHRASE11 (load_PHRASExx_HSQ, seg000:d00f).
]]]
attr[seg001:aad6]: type = u16; name = dialogue_phrase12_first_record_ptr; comment = [[[
    Boundary pointer at offset 0x60 inside the DIALOGUE buffer (seg001:aa76, resource 0xbd): the relocated near-offset of the first dialogue record belonging to the PHRASE12 bank.
    Set at startup by initialize_resources2: seg000:0120 HSQ-decompresses DIALOGUE in place via open_resource_force_hsq, leaving the raw offset 0x0930 here; seg000:0123 then calls adjust_sub_resource_pointers, whose stosw loop adds the buffer base 0aa76h to relocate it (0x0930 -> 0xb3a6, an address within the DIALOGUE buffer).
    load_PHRASExx_HSQ (seg000:d012) compares dialogue_current_record_ptr against it: below -> PHRASE11, at or above -> PHRASE12.
]]]
attr[seg001:ab6a]: type = u16
